From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:17:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Count the Apple A10 as supported

The A10 GPU needed exp_hw_support=1 to bind, which every installed
system had to set in modprobe configuration. The desktop runs on it
now, so it binds like the other supported cores. It still binds only
where its firmware is installed.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
index af1a61bdbb72..01bc08f7b84e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
@@ -538,10 +538,8 @@ pvr_gpu_support_level(const struct pvr_gpu_id *gpu_id)
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(33, 15, 11, 3):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 52, 104, 182):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 53, 104, 796):
-		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
-
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(13, 10, 6, 2):	/* Apple A10 (T8010) */
-		return PVR_GPU_EXPERIMENTAL;
+		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
 
 	default:
 		return PVR_GPU_UNKNOWN;
